# Sources of the study of the emitters written in the old body's own language (r2/gap-inlanguage-emitter). The runtime, its op table, the floor record and jit-page.bml are 2.1.6, 2.1.7, 2.1.10 and 2.1.14.

n: 2.17
name: in-language-emitter-sources
kind: hub
is: Sources cited by the study of the machine-code writers written in the old body's own language, read 2026-11-24: the study report, eleven program and test files of the old body, two of its documents and five private working notes. Three files of the leaf compiler's heat gate (2.17.21 to 2.17.23) were added by the review of 3.9. The runtime's C file, its operation table, the floor record and the page emitter jit-page.bml are cited from 2.1.6, 2.1.7, 2.1.10 and 2.1.14.
at: 2026-11-24
by: r2/gap-inlanguage-emitter

n: 2.17.1
name: gap-inlanguage-emitter.md
kind: source
is: The study report on the emitters written in the old body's language, 625 lines in 17 sections: the map of writers, what jit-page.bml compiles and declines, its frame and values, the helper table, offer and install, the encoders, the object writer, speeds and wrong answers on record, keep and let-go lists and a proposed minimal interface.
path: coherence-seed/study/r2/gap-inlanguage-emitter.md
date: 2026-11-24
got: 2026-11-24
at: 2026-11-24
by: r2/gap-inlanguage-emitter

n: 2.17.2
name: form-asm.fk
kind: source
is: The old body's AArch64 assembler as data rows, 306 lines: one generic packer and 71 instruction encoders that answer little-endian bytes. The study gives its last commit as 2026-10-12.
path: coherence-kernel/form/form-stdlib/form-asm.fk
